ExactMouse Redux — End User License Agreement

DRAFT FOR LEGAL REVIEW — NOT APPROVED FOR DISTRIBUTION.

Copyright © 2026 Maximilian Dahl. All rights reserved.

This English draft prepares terms for future proprietary releases. It must be
reviewed by qualified legal counsel, made publicly accessible, included with
the relevant distribution and validly agreed where required before use as
distribution terms. Publishing this draft does not change existing contracts,
establish user acceptance or start Pro sales.

1. Scope and agreement

This agreement is between Maximilian Dahl (the licensor) and the person or
organisation using ExactMouse Redux (the licensee). It applies only to future
versions distributed with these terms for which they have been validly agreed.
Installing, downloading, using or updating the app does not by itself establish
agreement to this draft. It does not apply retroactively.

ExactMouse Redux has been distributed as proprietary software since version
3.8.0. Existing valid licenses and entitlements remain in effect under their
applicable terms. Earlier open-license grants are preserved by section 4.

The proprietary software is licensed, not sold. Ownership of proprietary code
and assets remains with the relevant rights holders. You retain rights in your
own data and work.

2. Free features and permitted use

You receive a non-exclusive license to install and run ExactMouse Redux Free
on Macs you own or control for personal or business use, including commercial
work, without payment. You may make copies necessary for that use and backups.
This does not authorise distribution or resale of proprietary material to
others, subject to sections 4 and 5.

3. Pro and Early Access

Pro features are currently unlocked without payment during Early Access. This
draft does not require payment for that access or activate a checkout, paid
license check or trial.

Once Pro sales begin, use of paid Pro features in future releases requires a
valid Pro license. Before purchase, the offer must state the price, included
features, license duration, permitted users and installations, and any update
or renewal entitlements. This draft creates no subscription and promises no
lifetime updates. A Pro license may be used by the purchasing person or
organisation within the agreed entitlement, subject to applicable law.

Temporary Early Access does not itself promise that Pro features will remain
free in future releases. A future paid transition must respect statutory
rights, existing contracts, valid licenses and entitlements. It cannot create
retroactive payment obligations or reduce rights already granted in earlier
copies. A change to Pro does not itself authorise removal of contracted features;
any change must comply with applicable statutory and contractual requirements.

4. Earlier MIT releases and third-party material

Versions up to and including 3.7.5 were published under the MIT License.
Rights already granted under MIT remain in effect, including use, copying,
modification, distribution, sublicensing and sale, subject to its terms and
notice requirements. They are not limited to copies obtained before the
proprietary transition. This agreement does not revoke, narrow or replace those
grants, including for MIT-licensed portions reused in later releases. The original
MIT notice is preserved in the appendix and applies to that earlier material.

Third-party material retains its own licenses and copyright notices. Where an
applicable third-party license grants rights for a component, that license
governs the component. This draft grants no new MIT license for proprietary
material and does not claim ownership of third-party works.

5. Restrictions and statutory rights

For proprietary material not covered by section 4, you may not modify,
redistribute, publish, sublicense, rent, lend or sell the software, its source
code or its assets without prior written permission from Maximilian Dahl,
except as expressly permitted by this agreement, a separate applicable license
or law. Linking to the official download page is permitted.

Do not circumvent license controls or remove applicable copyright, trademark
or license notices, except where permitted by law or an applicable license.
Restrictions on modification, translation, reverse engineering, disassembly
and decompilation apply only to the extent permitted by applicable law.

These restrictions do not limit mandatory rights, including lawful backups,
observation, study, testing, interoperability, decompilation or exhaustion of
distribution rights to the extent applicable law protects them.

6. Updates and privacy

Updates may be offered through the app's update mechanism. This agreement does
not promise a release schedule, new features or indefinite support. Mandatory
update and other statutory obligations remain unaffected.

Different terms for a future version must be made available and validly agreed
where required. An automatic update is not automatic acceptance of different
terms and does not alter rights in earlier copies.

See LEGAL.md for the project's privacy and trademark notices. They do not
replace applicable third-party privacy information.

7. Warranty, liability and ending use

Statutory warranty, defect, liability and consumer rights apply. This draft
does not exclude or limit them and adds no separate contractual warranty.
Future Pro purchases must be accompanied by legally required information about
the seller, payment, withdrawal, remedies and support.

You may stop using the app and uninstall it at any time. Ending a proprietary
license for material breach requires a lawful basis and notice, including an
opportunity to remedy the breach where required. If that license lawfully
ends, stop using and remove copies covered by it, except where retention or
use is permitted by law or a separate license. Earlier MIT grants, existing
independent entitlements and third-party rights remain unaffected.

8. Trademarks

ExactMouse Redux is an independent, unofficial project. It is not affiliated
with, endorsed, sponsored or supported by SteelSeries ApS. SteelSeries and
ExactMouse are trademarks or registered trademarks of SteelSeries ApS. See
LEGAL.md for the existing attribution and trademark notice.

Maintainer prerequisites — not additional end-user terms

- Obtain legal review of ownership, contributor permissions, employment-related
  rights, and AI-assisted code and asset provenance and protectability;
  actual binary provenance and privacy behaviour; commercial use of
  the app name and SteelSeries trademarks (a disclaimer is not legal clearance);
  the MIT/proprietary boundary and reused portions; permitted users
  and installations; consumer rights, liability, termination and the languages
  required in the intended markets.
- Preserve the original MIT notice in the appendix and all applicable third-party
  notices with relevant distributions. Map reused portions across the 3.8.0
  transition against the source and archives; the public project repository no
  longer contains app source.
- Publish the reviewed terms and include them with downloads and the app.
  Check the private build, release, installer and update paths and implement
  valid presentation and agreement where required. The public installer
  currently contains no license presentation or agreement step.
  Reconcile embedded Help, localised license/privacy text and Pro-offer wording
  with the reviewed terms and actual behaviour before a release uses them.
- Before Pro sales, confirm the actual offer, seller/contact information,
  purchase and withdrawal disclosures and payment/license system. Assess provider
  identification and accurate, separate privacy disclosures for the actual data
  flows, including for the free edition. Review applicable electronic
  withdrawal-function requirements before enabling online sales. Review the
  implemented user-started seven-day trial and Early Access transition. No seller
  address, checkout provider, price, governing-law clause or court venue is
  supplied by this draft.

